.TH MVM 1 "2026-11-25" "mvm 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mvm \- run dev tooling in ephemeral Podman+krun microVMs with locked ext4 caches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mvm
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.B \-\-
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.br
.B mvm cache
.I SUBCOMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mvm
runs build tools, package managers, and untrusted scripts inside an ephemeral
hardware-virtualized microVM via
.BR podman (1)
with
.B \-\-runtime krun
(zero host privileges, no host namespaces).
.PP
By default:
.IP \(bu 2
Networking is disabled
.RB ( \-\-network=none ).
Pass
.B \-\-net
only when fetching dependencies.
.IP \(bu 2
The current working directory is bind-mounted read-only at
.I /src
with working directory
.IR /src .
Pass
.B \-\-rw
to mount it read-write, or
.B \-o DIR
to mount
.I ./DIR
read-write at
.IR /out .
.IP \(bu 2
Named sparse ext4 cache images under
.I ~/.cache/mvm/*.img
are loop-mounted inside the guest kernel and cleanly unmounted on exit.
This keeps compiler metadata churn off
.B virtio-fs
and reduces SELinux
.B :z
relabeling to a single inode per cache image.
.IP \(bu 2
Every cache image is automatically protected with
.BR flock (2)
on the host: shared lock
.RB ( LOCK_SH )
for read-only mounts and exclusive lock
.RB ( LOCK_EX )
for read-write mounts.
.SH PROFILES
Profiles select a default OCI image, memory limit, environment variables, and
ext4 cache images automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-go
Uses
.I docker.io/library/golang:1.27-alpine
(2g RAM,
.BR CGO_ENABLED=0 ),
mounts
.I go-mod
at
.I /cache/go-mod
(read-only offline, read-write with
.BR \-\-net ),
and
.I go-build
at
.I /cache/go-build
(read-write).
.TP
.B \-\-rust
Uses
.I docker.io/library/rust:1.98-alpine
(4g RAM,
.BR CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/cache/target ),
mounts
.I cargo-reg
at
.I /usr/local/cargo/registry
(read-only offline, read-write with
.BR \-\-net ),
and
.I cargo-target
at
.I /cache/target
(read-write).
.TP
.B \-\-node
Uses
.I docker.io/library/node:22-alpine
(2g RAM,
.BR npm_config_cache=/cache/npm ),
mounts
.I npm
at
.I /cache/npm
(read-write).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image " " \fIIMAGE\fR
OCI container image to run (overrides profile default).
.TP
.B \-\-net
Enable networking inside the microVM (default is
.BR \-\-network=none ).
Also upgrades profile dependency caches
.RI ( go-mod ", " cargo-reg )
from read-only to read-write.
.TP
.B \-\-rw
Mount the current directory read-write at
.I /src
instead of read-only.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " " \fIDIR\fR
Mount
.I ./DIR
read-write at
.I /out
(creating it on the host if needed) while keeping
.I /src
read-only.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mem " " \fISIZE\fR
MicroVM RAM limit (default:
.BR 2g ,
or
.B 4g
for
.BR \-\-rust ).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cache " " \fINAME\fR[\fB:ro\fR|\fB:rw\fR]\fB:\fIGUEST_PATH\fR
Attach a named ext4 cache image from
.I ~/.cache/mvm/NAME.img
and loop-mount it at
.I GUEST_PATH
inside the microVM. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tmpfs " " \fIGUEST_PATH\fR[\fB:\fISIZE\fR]
Mount an in-VM
.B tmpfs
at
.I GUEST_PATH
(default size
.BR 1g ).
Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-env " " \fIKEY\fR[\fB=\fIVAL\fR]
Pass an environment variable into the microVM. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-volume " " \fISPEC\fR
Pass an extra
.B podman \-v
bind mount specification. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-no-src
Do not mount the current working directory at
.IR /src .
.TP
.B \-\-crun
Fall back to a standard
.B crun
container instead of
.B krun
(incompatible with
.BR \-\-cache ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage summary and exit.
.SH CACHE MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B mvm cache ls
List cache images under
.I ~/.cache/mvm
with actual disk usage and virtual size.
.TP
.B mvm cache init \fINAME\fR [\fISIZE\fR]
Create a new empty sparse ext4 cache image (default virtual size:
.BR 4G ).
.TP
.B mvm cache import \fINAME\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR [\fISIZE\fR]
Populate a new sparse ext4 cache image from an existing host directory using
unprivileged
.BR mkfs.ext4 (8)
.BR \-d .
If
.I SIZE
is omitted, defaults to
.IR max(2G,\ 2\ *\ dir_size) .
.TP
.B mvm cache grow \fINAME\fR \fINEW_SIZE\fR
Expand a sparse ext4 cache image under an exclusive lock using
.BR truncate (1),
.BR e2fsck (8),
and
.BR resize2fs (8).
.TP
.B mvm cache rm \fINAME\fR
Remove a cache image and its lockfile.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Import existing host Go and Cargo caches:
.RS
.EX
mvm cache import go-mod ~/.cache/go-mod 2G
mvm cache import go-build ~/.cache/go-build 5G
mvm cache import cargo-reg ~/.cache/cargo 2G
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fetch dependencies with network, then build offline into
.IR ./build :
.RS
.EX
mvm --net --go -- go mod download
mvm --go -o build -- go build -trimpath -o /out/gateway ./cmd/gateway
.EE
.RE
.PP
Offline Rust release build:
.RS
.EX
mvm --rust -o build -- cargo build --offline --release
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run a one-off offline command with in-VM tmpfs scratch:
.RS
.EX
mvm -i docker.io/library/alpine:latest -t /tmp/work:1g -- sh -c 'df -h /tmp/work'
.EE
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MVM_CACHE_DIR
Override the cache image directory (default:
.IR ~/.cache/mvm ).
.TP
.B MVM_GO_IMAGE\fR, \fBMVM_RUST_IMAGE\fR, \fBMVM_NODE_IMAGE
Override default OCI images for built-in profiles.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/mvm
Executable script.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mvm/*.img
Sparse ext4 cache images.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mvm/*.lock
Host
.BR flock (2)
lockfiles for coordinating concurrent microVMs.
.SH CAVEATS
.IP \(bu 2
Writable ext4 cache images are single-writer; concurrent runs wait automatically
on
.BR flock (2).
Read-only caches
.RB ( :ro )
can be shared concurrently.
.IP \(bu 2
Inside
.B krun \-\-network=none
some loopback socket tests may behave differently than under
.BR crun .
Use
.B \-\-crun
(without ext4 cache images) or regular
.B podman run --rm --network=none
if a unit test hits a
.B krun
networking quirk.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR podman (1),
.BR mkfs.ext4 (8),
.BR flock (2)
